#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119640 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119829 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f5c9c30-1745-5986-b116-e9e70a7c6161" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Vector"}] :question/id #uuid "ba897e22-8104-5772-a0d3-9b062f3592f1" :question/math-academy-id "e-4932" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point $P(-3,2,1)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $\\mathbf{n}= \\langle 0, 2, 0 \\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $\\mathbf{p}=\\langle -3,2,1 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{n}=\\langle 0,2,0 \\rangle$ is normal to the plane.\n\nThe equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(x_0,y_0,z_0)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $\\mathbf{n}$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(\\mathbf{r} - \\mathbf{p}) \\cdot \\mathbf{n} = 0,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{r}$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $\\mathbf p$ is the position vector of $P.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,2,0⟩ & =⟨-3,2,1⟩\\cdot ⟨0,2,0⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,2,0⟩ & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119641 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119830 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0d93156-f9be-5e6e-976a-bef30dc892ee" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector That Is Parallel To a Plane"}] :question/id #uuid "a33f6c43-4e25-5d67-9f73-ca99a18fb434" :question/math-academy-id "e-4933" :question/problem "A nonzero vector $\\langle 0,\\, \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{b}, \\: \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{c} \\rangle$ is parallel to the plane $\\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\langle 2, -1, 4 \\rangle  = 3.$ What is the value of $\\dfrac{b}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need a vector $\\mathbf{v} = \\langle t_1,t_2,t_3 \\rangle$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $\\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\langle 2, -1, 4 \\rangle  = 3$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $\\mathbf{n}=\\langle 2, -1, 4 \\rangle.$ So, $\\mathbf{v} \\perp \\mathbf{n}$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨2,-1,4⟩ & =0 \\\\ 2{t}_{1}-{t}_{2}+4{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & =2{t}_{1}+4{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{v}=\\langle t_1, 2t_1 + 4t_3, t_3 \\rangle,\n$$\n\nwhere $t_1,t_3 \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$ \n\nWe are told that the first component of $\\mathbf{v}$ equals $0.$ So, we must set $t_1=0.$ \n\nSince $\\mathbf{v}$ is nonzero, we can pick any $t_3 \\neq 0.$ For example, setting $t_3=1$, we get\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{v} = \\langle 0,\\, \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{4}, \\, \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{1} \\rangle.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\dfrac{b}{c} = 4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119642 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119831 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "45cdbb0d-2986-5c05-8d23-dce29363051b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Straight Line"}] :question/id #uuid "43586a83-879c-5caf-9063-a8f4afbb8b4c" :question/math-academy-id "e-4935" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(\\sqrt{2},0,-5)$ and is perpendicular to the line\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3 \\\\ y=-1+\\sqrt{3}t \\\\ z=5-t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vector of $Q$ is $\\mathbf{q}=\\langle \\sqrt{2},0,-5 \\rangle.$ Converting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n![](images/3c/3c1e2e4034bcbc860f548935ca7305bc8f141c56ba14f821fd1aa6cb2b53f8d9.png)\n\nThe direction vector of the line is $\\mathbf{v}=\\langle  0 , \\sqrt{3} , -1\\rangle,$ so a normal vector to the plane is \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{n}=\\mathbf{v}=\\langle  0 , \\sqrt{3} , -1 \\rangle.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,\\sqrt{3},-1⟩ & =⟨\\sqrt{2},0,-5⟩\\cdot ⟨0,\\sqrt{3},-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,\\sqrt{3},-1⟩ & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262837 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119830 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0d93156-f9be-5e6e-976a-bef30dc892ee" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector That Is Parallel To a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1db4c2af-2e78-5ec5-8ede-f1aff92a3bae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260130} {:answer/id #uuid "4e4df1a9-277d-5ebc-8864-b31c9ef3bafa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260540} {:answer/id #uuid "86ae6e82-65b8-5c01-9bd6-0496eaf7bc36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261049} {:answer/id #uuid "b8ab9526-555f-538e-8473-1cc8d4c5b366" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261494} {:answer/id #uuid "f9ced82e-1eb9-51cb-8708-d7eb16c14606" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262056}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1db4c2af-2e78-5ec5-8ede-f1aff92a3bae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260130} :answer-field/id #uuid "40642ce9-2755-5ebb-8afd-84006382c910" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262238}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1e0d1c80-eb5c-5bda-b21b-a06adaec16d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-127873" :question/problem "A nonzero vector $⟨0,\\,b,\\,c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩=7.$ What is the value of $\\frac{b}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩=7$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-3,1,-2⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩ & =0 \\\\ -3{t}_{1}+{t}_{2}-2{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & =3{t}_{1}+2{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},\\,3{t}_{1}+2{t}_{3},\\,{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the first component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{1}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{3}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{3}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨0,\\,2,\\,1⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{b}{c}=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262846 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119830 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0d93156-f9be-5e6e-976a-bef30dc892ee" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector That Is Parallel To a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1066db60-12af-5e82-a7c0-d24afa450e35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260024} {:answer/id #uuid "336d23d9-d848-54ca-86e6-782c1b13a369" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260339} {:answer/id #uuid "6bfd83ea-5bb5-57e7-b814-e0e365ce1b44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260820} {:answer/id #uuid "d4093fa7-7b24-5445-bf63-718de7a82e0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261744} {:answer/id #uuid "f03309e1-ca15-5335-aab5-a2535a4337a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261981}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "336d23d9-d848-54ca-86e6-782c1b13a369" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260339} :answer-field/id #uuid "f46674a6-7e2b-5656-b018-7f5bf5e7afa0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262547}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aa3bed00-1af4-5c46-8c12-264209634c51" :question/math-academy-id "q-127910" :question/problem "A nonzero vector $⟨a,\\,0,\\,c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨-1,1,3⟩=\\sqrt{7}.$ What is the value of $\\frac{a}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨-1,1,3⟩=\\sqrt{7}$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-1,1,3⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,1,3⟩ & =0 \\\\ -{t}_{1}+{t}_{2}+3{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{1} & ={t}_{2}+3{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{2}+3{t}_{3},\\,{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{2},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the second component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{2}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{3}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{3}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨3,\\,0,\\,1⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{a}{c}=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262857 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119831 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "45cdbb0d-2986-5c05-8d23-dce29363051b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Straight Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a6d49af-f4b3-58b7-98b0-926d7d2ec1bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-4,3⟩=15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259966} {:answer/id #uuid "bfef5be5-9f0c-5938-9df5-2b2093f08bac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-3,4,1⟩=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261571} {:answer/id #uuid "c1b1b7f5-3316-5749-a268-d9545bd6066b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-4,3,1⟩=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261585} {:answer/id #uuid "cbe23397-9a20-5f8a-922d-81c869029405" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨3,1,4⟩=13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261671} {:answer/id #uuid "da6e68b1-4c37-525a-a289-ddc6a1494083" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,4,3⟩=11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261805}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bfef5be5-9f0c-5938-9df5-2b2093f08bac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-3,4,1⟩=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261571} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f2421e2-84aa-5ab7-a62e-bbab5487c4bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262408}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cf1b6add-bb69-5029-a7d5-1bf17a1142b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-127944" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(-1,1,2)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=5-3t \\\\ y=2+4t \\\\ z=-3+t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨-1,1,2⟩.$ Converting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=5-3t \\\\ y=2+4t \\\\ z=-3+t\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,⟨x,y,z⟩=⟨5,2,-3⟩+t\\text{ }{{⟨-3,4,1⟩}_{⏟}}_{v}.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe direction vector of the line is $v=⟨-3,4,1⟩,$ so a normal vector to the plane is \n\n$$\nn=v=⟨-3,4,1⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-3,4,1⟩ & =⟨-1,1,2⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,4,1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-3,4,1⟩ & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262859 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119831 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "45cdbb0d-2986-5c05-8d23-dce29363051b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Straight Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65e4dacb-b64f-5663-ae54-844ec9e37c4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-2,4⟩=22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260760} {:answer/id #uuid "a344d6d0-c843-57a0-87ed-6643487a6ce9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-2,2,1⟩=12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261298} {:answer/id #uuid "a5b752a4-52ea-54e2-96dc-81dc14098d76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨4,-2,1⟩=18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261313} {:answer/id #uuid "aa9815dd-2b59-5495-91a4-c387e6882786" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-4,-2⟩=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261371} {:answer/id #uuid "c0f71bee-c234-59c3-9e78-d739bf030e68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,-2,1⟩=15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261577}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0f71bee-c234-59c3-9e78-d739bf030e68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,-2,1⟩=15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261577} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e498358-75ca-5ef1-ae02-06dee6634086" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262265}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7885abf5-baa7-59dd-be20-bec3451c5be4" :question/math-academy-id "q-127956" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(4,-2,3)$ and is  perpendicular to the line \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1+2t \\\\ y=3-2t \\\\ z=5+t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨4,-2,3⟩.$ Converting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1+2t \\\\ y=3-2t \\\\ z=5+t\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,⟨x,y,z⟩=⟨-1,3,5⟩+t\\text{ }{{⟨2,-2,1⟩}_{⏟}}_{v}.\n$$\n\n   \n\nThe direction vector of the line is $v=⟨2,-2,1⟩.$ So, a normal  vector to the plane is \n\n$$\nn=v=⟨2,-2,1⟩.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,-2,1⟩ & =⟨4,-2,3⟩\\cdot ⟨2,-2,1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,-2,1⟩ & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304808 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119829 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f5c9c30-1745-5986-b116-e9e70a7c6161" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1aa5c8f6-bf83-5bd8-9bb3-80811ef65a96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302631} {:answer/id #uuid "407d1ed1-6ab5-5fde-b2e9-9ef394359c42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302860} {:answer/id #uuid "42cce788-2ef2-5bc9-89b5-61bb8342b033" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302878} {:answer/id #uuid "4a24ce80-8c12-5476-97ef-85e573270172" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302924} {:answer/id #uuid "a92599b3-9f56-5635-b79f-2c71088e3569" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303499}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1aa5c8f6-bf83-5bd8-9bb3-80811ef65a96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302631} :answer-field/id #uuid "6581d869-7e78-5398-89d1-33179a6e2c3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304351}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "62f6f273-804e-559c-a53a-0d8f68234b8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-33027" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point $Q(1,2,-1)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ and $n=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ is normal to the plane.\n\nThe equation of the plane that passes though the point $Q({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(r-q)\\cdot n=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $q$ is the position vector of $Q.$\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304818 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119829 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f5c9c30-1745-5986-b116-e9e70a7c6161" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "557e38a7-a029-588d-bfe3-065970b42e29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot (i-\\sqrt{3}j+4k)=8i+\\sqrt{27}j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302983} {:answer/id #uuid "7b5e4122-6bcd-5d0f-81a6-b8727f7f80bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot (i-\\sqrt{3}j+4k)=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303218} {:answer/id #uuid "dcdc9b30-9726-5982-8b3e-a81f38639057" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot (8i+\\sqrt{27}j)=i-\\sqrt{3}j+4k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303836} {:answer/id #uuid "f1d19671-a68e-5384-b817-7d3c1d7cbc20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot (8i+\\sqrt{27}j)=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303975} {:answer/id #uuid "fc41c2f2-2231-5ddb-adb6-644582d77c1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot (8i+\\sqrt{27}j)=8-\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304038}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1d19671-a68e-5384-b817-7d3c1d7cbc20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot (8i+\\sqrt{27}j)=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303975} :answer-field/id #uuid "39ef42cb-e415-5101-9065-d75c9c30b48d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304232}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cd3baba0-1430-5e29-b123-dd1e840723b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-33035" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point  $P(1,-\\sqrt{3},4)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=8i+\\sqrt{27}j.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=i-\\sqrt{3}j+4k$ and $n=8i+\\sqrt{27}j$ is normal to the plane.\n\nThe equation of the plane that passes through the point $P({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n$ can be given as \n\n$$\n(r-p)\\cdot n=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $p$ is the position vector of $P.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot (8i+\\sqrt{27}j) & =(i-\\sqrt{3}j+4k)\\cdot (8i+\\sqrt{27}j) \\\\ r\\cdot (8i+\\sqrt{27}j) & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308389 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119830 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0d93156-f9be-5e6e-976a-bef30dc892ee" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector That Is Parallel To a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2be2860e-76f3-5d9d-bf88-ce7854d1a186" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305571} {:answer/id #uuid "6c6f1eb0-ee64-514d-98de-d34d9b44314a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306190} {:answer/id #uuid "7b28870c-c686-56de-8301-a1d3a6669a64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306326} {:answer/id #uuid "7b563320-dadf-52e8-ae03-48cf4482b401" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306330} {:answer/id #uuid "e06638bf-2fdd-5ef3-8ff6-f99f8daca96b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307227}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2be2860e-76f3-5d9d-bf88-ce7854d1a186" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305571} :answer-field/id #uuid "f682525d-3133-53f0-ba43-839c46ba42eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308303}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a973cbbd-df7e-5f41-a87c-5c205b31db4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-33313" :question/problem "A nonzero vector $⟨a,\\,0,\\,c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨4,0,2⟩=16.$ What is the value of $\\frac{a}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨4,0,2⟩=16$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨4,0,2⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨4,0,2⟩ & =0 \\\\ 4{t}_{1}+2{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ 2{t}_{3} & =-4{t}_{1} \\\\ {t}_{3} & =-2{t}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},\\,{t}_{2},\\,-2{t}_{1}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{2}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the second component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{2}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{1}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{1}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨1,\\,0,\\,-2⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{a}{c}=-\\frac{1}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120247 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119831 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "45cdbb0d-2986-5c05-8d23-dce29363051b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Straight Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94e18650-280a-5354-a406-fb0defcb81aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r \\cdot ⟨ - 4, 6, 2⟩ = ⟨ - 2, 2, 0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117642} {:answer/id #uuid "d4d90d97-d648-5e9e-b848-063a15214b98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r \\cdot ⟨ - 4, 6, 2⟩ = 20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117643} {:answer/id #uuid "29900cd3-7de8-5138-a84e-15303e431cef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r \\cdot ⟨ - 2, 2, 0⟩ = ⟨ - 4, 6, 2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117644} {:answer/id #uuid "52057ada-186e-58b1-9f7e-330d431687c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r \\cdot ⟨ - 4, 6, 2⟩ = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117645} {:answer/id #uuid "5d6bda8f-e81f-5158-9056-39a949f8f7cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r \\cdot ⟨ - 2, 2, 0⟩ = 20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117646}] :answer-field/id #uuid "34844c94-379b-5d2b-9891-556e1746b8f9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117641} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72c2e5ca-f263-54ef-924a-e167ca91f89b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-2,2,0⟩=⟨-4,6,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363753} {:answer/id #uuid "32d8e4c3-ddfe-54ee-ae03-e8de00c5efb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-2,2,0⟩=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363754} {:answer/id #uuid "730f759e-812a-532c-8ba9-65f2916ee485" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-4,6,2⟩=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363755} {:answer/id #uuid "9471d411-f775-5f03-a79f-1eb639079ffa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-4,6,2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363756} {:answer/id #uuid "1f6058f7-7b71-5d3e-a88e-644aa57521b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-4,6,2⟩=⟨-2,2,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363757}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "730f759e-812a-532c-8ba9-65f2916ee485" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-4,6,2⟩=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363755} :answer-field/id #uuid "12ab60fb-0ccd-54c4-b8b9-1cf65f373926" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363752}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8a0ae68a-8650-5549-af6c-052d2786d395" :question/math-academy-id "q-33316" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(-2,2,0)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3-4t \\\\ y=1+6t \\\\ z=-1+2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨-2,2,0⟩.$ Converting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3-4t \\\\ y=1+6t \\\\ z=-1+2t\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,⟨x,y,z⟩=⟨3,1,-1⟩+t\\text{ }{{⟨-4,6,2⟩}_{⏟}}_{v}.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe direction vector of the line is $v=⟨-4,6,2⟩,$ so a normal vector to the plane is \n\n$$\nn=v=⟨-4,6,2⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-4,6,2⟩ & =⟨-2,2,0⟩\\cdot ⟨-4,6,2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-4,6,2⟩ & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308399 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119831 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "45cdbb0d-2986-5c05-8d23-dce29363051b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Straight Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "166ef2d2-32f9-5566-82ce-7cdba329c024" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305351} {:answer/id #uuid "2d1369ba-d6af-518c-9a18-2bcb2250fd78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩=-23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305582} {:answer/id #uuid "60c376f1-f147-5aa7-8c7c-ae55262553b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩=⟨1,-4,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306084} {:answer/id #uuid "872e10d1-c31a-5bdc-a18f-00aeaf508a92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-4,2⟩=⟨-1,5,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306439} {:answer/id #uuid "d788f251-5e9e-56e8-8b45-aa84f1099d81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-4,2⟩=-23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307146}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d1369ba-d6af-518c-9a18-2bcb2250fd78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩=-23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305582} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fc16c6a-1a25-557e-b7df-b3323cb169a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307974}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4553242a-e32b-5422-9dd6-251f47f5a320" :question/math-academy-id "q-33317" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(1,-4,2)$ and is perpendicular to the line that goes through the points \n$A(2,1,-3)$ and $B(1,6,-4).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨1,-4,2⟩.$\n\nSince the line  passes through the points $A(2,1,-3)$ and $B(1,6,-4)$ we can find a vector parallel to the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨1,6,-4⟩-⟨2,1,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,5,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-1,5,-1⟩.$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩ & =⟨1,-4,2⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩ & =-23.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308412 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119829 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f5c9c30-1745-5986-b116-e9e70a7c6161" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3aef8723-641e-516c-8c4a-a5d5de549a58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot (5i+2j+3k)=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305710} {:answer/id #uuid "9813abc0-1700-54c0-9c07-5981bf1e93ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot (5i+2j+3k)=52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306578} {:answer/id #uuid "ba6412aa-de58-53f9-bd92-3970bea844c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot (6i+5j+4k)=5i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306890} {:answer/id #uuid "d3ef5d7c-8f43-5fb9-88cc-0e631dbc7945" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot (6i+5j+4k)=52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307114} {:answer/id #uuid "d401246f-9f18-5c5b-9df7-2bc112841ad2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot (6i+5j+4k)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307117}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3ef5d7c-8f43-5fb9-88cc-0e631dbc7945" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot (6i+5j+4k)=52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307114} :answer-field/id #uuid "d63df9bb-7280-5cd8-aee8-407814fcba8f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308192}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dc9756ae-93f4-5e8e-b7df-21ca51316b9d" :question/math-academy-id "q-33322" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point  $Q(5,2,3)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=6i+5j+4k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=5i+2j+3k$ and $n=6i+5j+4k$ is normal to the plane. \n\nThe equation of the plane that passes though the point $Q({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(r-q)\\cdot n=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $q$ is the position vector of $Q.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot (6i+5j+4k) & =(5i+2j+3k)\\cdot (6i+5j+4k) \\\\ r\\cdot (6i+5j+4k) & =52.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338829 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119830 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0d93156-f9be-5e6e-976a-bef30dc892ee" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector That Is Parallel To a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46a8c73e-1b6f-5ead-8b4e-04fd47ae71ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336688} {:answer/id #uuid "566ad7e4-2332-5818-b1ab-63f151123755" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336827} {:answer/id #uuid "6955aab1-e2a7-5bda-a291-b54a99b1d9fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336968} {:answer/id #uuid "806b2ca4-42eb-53b0-90bb-44522d3b01e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337195} {:answer/id #uuid "d93906ff-8ee7-57c5-a797-f2d48eaf72f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337922}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46a8c73e-1b6f-5ead-8b4e-04fd47ae71ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336688} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac53d05e-4ae9-5aad-8699-2cdc5ab0d589" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338592}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3c12dba6-0a5e-5abe-ba85-6c6b625059ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-70822" :question/problem "A nonzero vector $⟨a,\\,b,\\,0⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨-5,-1,4⟩=6.$ What is the value of $\\frac{a}{b}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨-5,-1,4⟩=6$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-5,-1,4⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨-5,-1,4⟩ & =0 \\\\ -5{t}_{1}-{t}_{2}+4{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & =-5{t}_{1}+4{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},-5{t}_{1}+4{t}_{3},{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the third component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{3}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{1}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{1}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨1,\\,-5,\\,0⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{a}{b}=-\\frac{1}{5}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338830 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119830 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0d93156-f9be-5e6e-976a-bef30dc892ee" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector That Is Parallel To a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e4dafb7-c1e3-52bb-9be6-8c920a5e0c22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336620} {:answer/id #uuid "8adc6dd8-06c3-54d2-9922-36b4707070b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337284} {:answer/id #uuid "9a72c942-01f6-5ae4-80c1-9074296dcd5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337434} {:answer/id #uuid "bac2e877-851a-58b5-bda5-b1f53f68e73a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337687} {:answer/id #uuid "f5b3af4d-d5d3-54b2-80fd-fb6b4c38bce6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338180}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8adc6dd8-06c3-54d2-9922-36b4707070b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337284} :answer-field/id #uuid "f28575a2-8621-51a3-b18b-ae5aadfa4d66" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338700}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "31208d04-81a2-5a09-afcd-1cbba801d10f" :question/math-academy-id "q-70828" :question/problem "A nonzero vector $⟨0,\\,b,c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨-2,2,-4⟩=15.$ What is the value of $\\frac{b}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨-2,2,-4⟩=15$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-2,2,-4⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,2,-4⟩ & =0 \\\\ -2{t}_{1}+2{t}_{2}-4{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ 2{t}_{2} & =2{t}_{1}+4{t}_{3} \\\\ {t}_{2} & ={t}_{1}+2{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},\\,{t}_{1}+2{t}_{3},\\,{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the first component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{1}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{3}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{3}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨0,\\,2,\\,1⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{b}{c}=2.$"}]}
